    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1843">

                <pb facs="1351" n="1235" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1235"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.1052/54.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Price to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 24, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Supplementing my despatch 680 of October 17. Minister for Foreign Affairs in a
                    conversation declares that they will refuse to either sell or deliver to us the
                    police rifles, claiming they have given sufficiently strict orders to preclude
                    their use again in riots.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Price.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
